WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.135
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.137
we wanted to find the
differences between MREs

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.573
and ration packs in the US and the UK.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.707
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:14.080
A US MRE is manufactured and packaged

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.651
by Wornick, AmeriQual, and Sopakco

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.620
and comes in one standard pack size.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.089
UK MREs, or ration packs, as we call them,

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.657
are produced by Vestey Foods

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.192
and come in three portion sizes.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.229
The standard portion is
this, a 24-hour ration pack.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.897
You can also get a smaller version,

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.432
which is a 12-hour ration pack,

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.768
and our biggest portion

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.869
is this.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.104
This is a 10-man operational pack,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.241
which contains 10 of these
24-hour ration packs.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.610
According to the Defense
Logistics Agency website,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.512
a case of MREs, which is 12 meals,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:49.082
weighs around 22 pounds,
or 9.98 kilograms.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:53.953
So on average, one meal
would be roughly 831.6 grams.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.822
The approximate weight of
one of these ration packs

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.524
is 1.75 kilograms.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.225
We're going to weigh it
to see if that's accurate.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.998
So, the weight of our 24-hour ration pack

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.934
here in the UK was
actually 1.49 kilograms.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.470
This is a bit lower
than the promised 1.75.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.971
I don't know if you're
a soldier in the field

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.373
if this is actually a positive thing

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.308
because you've got less
weight to carry or if you're

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.077
actually getting slightly less
food than you were promised.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.945
In the UK, our ration pack menu No. 2

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.380
contains a chili con carne.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.115
We're going to compare
ours to the American chili

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.416
to see who's getting more.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.090
I do think I've lost a little bit in here.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.659
And if I were eating this
straight out of the packet,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.928
maybe tearing the packet
open, getting better access,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.831
I could probably get that
closer to the 300 mark.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.899
So, here are the contents
of a 24-hour ration pack

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:40.733
in the UK.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.069
In total, we counted 29 edible items

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.271
as well as a few extra
bits, including tissues,

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.674
sanitary wipes, matches,
and other stuff like that.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.844
Joe: We counted 11 edible
items in our US ration pack.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.982
Here are all the military MREs for the US

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.517
not available in the UK.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.119
And here are all the
ration packs in the UK

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.720
that you can't find in the US.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.522
There's actually very few overlap

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:06.292
of specific meals in US MREs
and the UK ration packs.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.696
Also, depending on which MRE meal you get,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.499
they contain different
combinations of snacks and sides.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.801
In both countries, official
MREs are not available

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.536
for sale directly to consumers.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.238
Basically, when you get
a ration pack in the UK,

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.340
it will come with a
corresponding menu number.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.975
The menu number will give
you a rough indication

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.042
of what you're going to find inside,

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.511
although there is a bit of variation.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.312
So, what we've done here
is lay out the breakfast

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.948
and the main-course options
in order of the menus.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.083
In the UK, we're currently able

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.252
to get hold of menus one to 10.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.521
All right. We got the US MREs.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.589
I think we got every menu, one through 24.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.158
We're going to go through the entrées

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.659
and the breakfasts now.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.328
I want to point out that for the US MREs,

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.598
not every single one came
with a definitive breakfast,

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.933
and some of them just had something

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.868
that was fruit or fruit-related,

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.137
which we assumed was supposed to be eaten

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.539
first thing in the morning.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.674
Now, all of these can be
eaten either hot or cold.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.376
I guess ideally, you'd
have them heated up.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.245
We actually got sent this
flameless heating bag.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.813
Instructions for use.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.149
This is either going to go really well

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.284
or I'm going to give myself

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.953
and the "Food Wars" table
some chemical burns.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.221
I'm going to do a chili
because we've already

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.123
got a chili opened and I kind
of know what they taste like.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.624
Filter line only.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.227
And then leave that for 10 minutes.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.061
Oh.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.734
Well, it works. [laughs]

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.169
I hope I've sealed that well enough,

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.605
because that steamed
up very quickly there.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.207
So, while that does its thing,
I guess all that remains

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:28.741
is for me to try the rest of them.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:31.578
Starting down here, remember
our good friend the chili?

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:35.148
Not bad. I would say as
average as chili can be.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.216
I think, honestly,

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:39.118
I've never been in the military,
I haven't done any service,

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.454
but I used to camp a lot when I was a kid,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.689
and I do remember going on

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:46.426
sometimes two-, three-week-long
canoe trips in Canada.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.895
Couple days in, this is, like, gourmet.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.129
You know what I'm talking about.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.332
Like, your standards change quickly

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.833
when you're outside all day.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.468
It comes with a cornbread.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.937
This cornbread muffin's
actually really good.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.339
Let's try it with the chili.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.774
So, the breakfast that we got for menu one

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.510
was pork sausage and
beans in a tomato sauce.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.280
This is kind of an iconic
British meal. I can't lie.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.915
It's kind of good.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.617
We're starting off strong. I like that.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:12.619
Next up, we have a pindi chana aloo,

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.821
which seems to be a
potato and chickpea curry.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.523
And then the final option
from menu one in the UK,

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.758
meatballs and pasta.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.894
Do I have high or low expectations
for meatballs and pasta?

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.062
Yeah, I mean,

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.064
I think my fear was that,
like, pasta doesn't hold up

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.200
very well when it's kind of submerged

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.801
in a sauce and cooked for a while,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.637
and I think that's kind of come true.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:31.504
Meatballs are all right, though.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.273
Menu No. 2, shredded
beef in barbecue sauce,

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:36.576
but also came with seasoned
black beans and tortillas.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.877
So, I mean,

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.012
I don't know how you would do this

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:43.750
out in the field with no
plates and not a table.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.985
And then the beans.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.221
A military taco. Here we go.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.523
These beans are rock solid.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.991
The consistency's a little weird.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:55.428
This one is the chicken and noodles

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.997
with vegetables in sauce.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.733
Yeah, this looks like a

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.303
can of, like, chunky soup

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.138
or chunky stew before you heat it up.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.639
This definitely should
be heated up before.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.541
And this smell — oh,
my God, this is brutal.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.375
If you had this

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.277
and you couldn't heat it
up for some reason ...

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.545
This is very bad.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:13.846
The first potential breakfast,

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.782
the applesauce with raspberry puree.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:16.816
Now we're talking here.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:21.120
Oh, my God, that does
not taste like fruit.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.822
That tastes like pure sugar.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.990
There is fruit in it,

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.827
but it tastes more like
fruit-flavored soda.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.429
This will definitely wake
you up in the morning.

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.263
Then we're on to menu two,

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:33.566
and the breakfast is a
raspberry muesli with milk.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.702
Now, it says "with milk," but
there is no liquid in here.

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.003
So I think what they've
done is actually put

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:39.372
powdered milk in here,
and you add some water,

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:40.440
and then hopefully that kind of

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.442
turns into something resembling milk.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:45.211
It looks very chalky and powdery

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.913
at the moment, without the water in it.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:49.682
It says to add around 100 mils of water,

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.752
mix it, and then leave it
to stand for a minute or so.

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:55.922
But yeah. I mean, now that's
looking a lot more like muesli.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:59.192
That's actually not bad.
I'm quite impressed by that.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.760
There is a slightly noticeable difference

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.295
between that and real milk.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:03.763
Then the mains for menu two,

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.165
obviously the chili con carne,

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.401
which we opened for the
portion-sizes section.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.902
Not the best visuals,

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:13.840
but it's quite hard to make a
nice-looking chili anyway, so,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.541
it's more about the taste.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.577
It's not spicy. Pretty well seasoned.

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:20.046
And then menu two also has a rajma masala.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.180
The longer I leave this one,

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.081
I think this is the first one

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.150
that has actually a bit of heat to it,

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.120
but not unpleasant at all,
just a nice warmth there.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.121
This hits close to home.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:31.457
Spaghetti with beef and sauce.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:35.161
Oh, and it even came
with Italian breadsticks.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.996
What do we think? It's not meatballs.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:39.766
They had meatballs. We
only have meat sauce.

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:40.933
Breadsticks.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.402
They're a bit dry.

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:44.937
They're the most driest
thing I've ever eaten.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.139
These are so dry.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:47.473
White chicken chunks.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:50.343
Oh, no! It's just, look.

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.446
Yeah, just canned white chicken.

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:58.951
No, I would be so bummed.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.253
Yeah, this is the worst one.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:04.323
So, we got a beef taco
filling with Santa Fe rice.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:09.662
Um, not horrible. Decent
seasoning, but yeah,

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.931
I think what's missing
for all these is cheese.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:12.799
Then we're on to menu three,

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:14.667
and we have our first duplicate item.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.202
It's another muesli for breakfast.

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:17.203
Now, this one, I'm intrigued by.

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.871
One of the main options in menu three,

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.274
steak and vegetables with dumplings.

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:23.342
A classic British beef stew

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.111
is kind of one of my favorite foods.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.813
Having said that, I've opened this,

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.514
and it looks and smells like cat food.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.783
Now, I've been eating most of
these straight out of the bag

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.152
because they've had a kind of
texture which permits that,

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:35.288
but this one I think we're
going to have to plate up.

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:40.193
This apparently is steak and
vegetables with dumplings.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.427
Now, I started this section by saying

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:43.262
that all of these can
be eaten hot or cold,

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:44.430
and I do think that's true.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.232
I guess the question is
whether or not all of them

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.301
should be eaten hot or cold.

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:51.037
And I think this one, just
immediately from the look of it,

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:52.805
I think probably needs to be heated up

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:57.543
because we've had our first
womp-womp moment of the episode.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:00.646
[womp womp]

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:01.481
That's not good.

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:04.083
Beef strips in a savory tomato sauce.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.519
Marinara sauce with meatballs.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:09.755
Wait, so there's no noodles?
Just sauce and meatballs?

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.625
Oh, my goodness. Look how
little these meatballs are.

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:13.459
Look at these little guys.

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.628
There's no pasta in
there, just the meatballs.

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:18.164
Yeah, ooh. SpaghettiO
level of meat flavor.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:21.000
Beef stew. Oh, at least
this one has noodles.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.804
And this one came with a "breakfast"

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:26.405
that was grape jelly.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:27.773
We're going to jump ahead
slightly to menu eight

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.243
because that's where I've
taken our hot main from.

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:31.177
And the alarm has just gone off,

00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:32.378
which means it's ready to eat.

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:35.114
Once it's cooked, just tear it along here,

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:36.849
and then it's at the perfect height

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:39.719
that you can then just also tear this

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:40.887
and eat the whole thing.

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:43.289
It's changed the consistency
of this a little bit.

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:45.625
I think with the steak and
vegetables, for example,

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.827
I think that would change
the consistency a lot,

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:49.128
whereas this has just made it

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:51.364
a little bit more runny, but not too bad.

00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:53.165
That was very hot, but
that's still really good.

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:55.134
I think this one I do
prefer heated up, actually.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:56.802
It brings out a few more of the flavors,

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:58.471
a little bit more depth of flavor to it.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:08:59.639
That's really good, and I'm so impressed

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:01.307
with this heating-pad thing.

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:05.611
The heating pad, as well as
just, I guess, warmed-up meals.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:06.946
Thumbs up from me so far.

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:09.415
Macaroni in a beef
sauce. Well, that's good.

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:12.118
We got noodles! And the chili.

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:14.487
Oh, that's terrible. It
doesn't taste like anything.

00:09:14.487 --> 00:09:15.988
Vegetarian taco pasta,

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:19.959
which is a vegetable crumble
with pasta in taco-style sauce.

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:23.796
Is this supposed to be "Zapplesauce"?

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:25.698
Who doesn't love a little applesauce?

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:28.968
Again, wow, super sweet.

00:09:28.968 --> 00:09:31.537
With sugar, not high-fructose
corn syrup, so that's a plus.

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.005
And the last item from menu three

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:35.508
is a beef burrito-style filling with rice.

00:09:35.508 --> 00:09:38.744
Sadly, this does not
come with any tortillas,

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:40.513
so you can't make an
actual burrito with it.

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:41.581
There's a little bit more spice

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.215
than anything else that I've had so far.

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:44.317
The texture of the rice

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:46.018
would be improved by heating this one up

00:09:46.018 --> 00:09:48.654
because the rice is still
a little bit al dente.

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:50.590
Elbow macaroni in tomato sauce.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.658
Granted, I mean, I know
I gotta heat them up.

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:54.026
Yeah, this one's all right.

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:56.762
Mango peach applesauce.
I'm liking the applesauce.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.431
This would be considered,
I guess, a breakfast,

00:09:58.431 --> 00:09:59.699
or ... it's fruity,

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:02.001
so maybe this you would
have first thing in the day.

00:10:02.001 --> 00:10:03.736
Ooh, yeah. Ooh, this is really good.

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:04.804
Next up, we've got menu four,

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:06.739
and we're starting with
an all-day breakfast.

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.274
Apparently it differs
from the sausage and beans

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:09.909
because this contains some omelet

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:11.577
as well as some bacon pieces.

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:14.547
I think my only criticism
of this is that the sauce

00:10:14.547 --> 00:10:16.716
that they put the beans
in is exceptionally sweet.

00:10:16.716 --> 00:10:17.850
Carrying on through menu four,

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.219
we have a pasta Bolognese main.

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:22.788
I have a similar concern
to the meatballs and pasta.

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:24.256
I think that is roughly the color

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:26.926
that you want your Bolognese
sauce to look like.

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:29.462
I think when I looked at this
one, I was expecting worse.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.197
Again, the vibe I'm getting,

00:10:31.197 --> 00:10:33.699
particularly from the pasta dishes,

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.401
is very much tinned-pasta vibe,

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:36.502
like a tinned Bolognese.

00:10:36.502 --> 00:10:37.670
And the last menu-four item

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:40.272
is a chicken curry with potatoes and rice.

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:42.341
There's actual decent-sized pieces

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:44.276
of what I hope is chicken.

00:10:44.276 --> 00:10:46.512
Less flavorful than
some of the other ones.

00:10:46.512 --> 00:10:47.980
I want to try heating some of these up.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:52.051
You do this. And then
you put your MRE inside.

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:54.086
Sorry, if you can't tell,
we're adding water to this.

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:55.054
Here we go.

00:10:55.054 --> 00:10:56.856
Real exciting stuff here in the studio!

00:10:56.856 --> 00:10:58.424
While we're moving on,

00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:00.860
so, we got one, two, three heating up.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.763
The staff was able to make
this thing work. I was not.

00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:05.564
I don't know why. We're moving on.

00:11:05.564 --> 00:11:10.202
We have a cheese tortellini
in a tomato sauce.

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:11.003
Oh, yeah, look at this.

00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:13.706
They got the whole tortellini right there.

00:11:13.706 --> 00:11:14.940
Then we're on to menu five,

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.742
and we're starting off
with another muesli.

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:18.878
It's the third muesli
we've had in five meals.

00:11:18.878 --> 00:11:20.079
The variation, I think, is going to

00:11:20.079 --> 00:11:21.480
start to kind of run dry.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.882
Speaking of a lack of variation,

00:11:22.882 --> 00:11:25.418
meal five also has
another pasta Bolognese.

00:11:25.418 --> 00:11:27.086
The different option from meal five

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:29.488
is a sweet and sour chicken with rice.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:33.359
Good color on it. Nice
familiar orange color.

00:11:33.359 --> 00:11:35.661
There's pineapple in
this. And water chestnuts.

00:11:35.661 --> 00:11:37.596
I'm kind of impressed.
This is pretty good.

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:38.898
I'd say this leans more on the balance

00:11:38.898 --> 00:11:41.100
of sweet rather than sweet and sour.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.334
I think with the water chestnut

00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:44.170
and also the pineapple chunks,

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.604
there's still some things
in there with bite,

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:46.439
which I appreciate.

00:11:46.439 --> 00:11:49.041
Creamy spinach fettuccine
with egg noodles,

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:51.711
spinach, and mushroom in a cream sauce.

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:54.080
Ugh.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.016
it feels like they're going a little,

00:11:57.016 --> 00:11:58.017
I don't want to say overboard

00:11:58.017 --> 00:11:59.819
because I figure you gotta
have a variety of meals,

00:11:59.819 --> 00:12:02.822
but doesn't a fettuccine with
mushrooms in a cream sauce,

00:12:02.822 --> 00:12:05.257
like, after a long day of

00:12:05.257 --> 00:12:07.193
hauling stuff around and soldiering

00:12:07.193 --> 00:12:10.429
and exhausting job and
carrying all this stuff,

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:11.797
just being like, "Ah, let's kick back

00:12:11.797 --> 00:12:15.334
with some spinach, mushrooms
in a cream sauce," like.

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:17.403
The most colorful one so far.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:20.272
I don't feel great. I do not feel good.

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:21.173
Next up is menu six,

00:12:21.173 --> 00:12:23.008
which we've actually
covered all of already.

00:12:23.008 --> 00:12:25.311
Starts with an all-day
breakfast, which I've had,

00:12:25.311 --> 00:12:27.880
then moves on to another pasta Bolognese,

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:31.283
which I've also had, and
finishes with my old friend

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:33.652
steak vegetables with dumplings,

00:12:33.652 --> 00:12:35.654
which I will absolutely
not be trying again.

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:39.091
This should be the
Mexican-style chicken stew.

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:40.259
Oh, and then they're saying

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:42.795
there's another "Tear
here to remove the MRE."

00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:45.698
Very smart. So you got
a second spot to tear.

00:12:45.698 --> 00:12:48.200
This is really smart. Second spot to tear.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.238
So it's easier just to grab the MRE out.

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:56.008
All right, so the package is hot,

00:12:56.008 --> 00:12:57.877
so it feels like this is much ...

00:12:57.877 --> 00:12:59.712
kind of smooshing around a little bit.

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:02.281
So, they are still flimsy tortillas,

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:04.817
but it looks like they're
chipotle flavored.

00:13:04.817 --> 00:13:06.752
Not as gelatinous, I guess.

00:13:08.087 --> 00:13:09.755
Definitely better heated up.

00:13:09.755 --> 00:13:11.624
Yeah, I like this. It's pretty good.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:12.725
Next up is menu seven,

00:13:12.725 --> 00:13:14.360
which, I don't know if
this was deliberate or not,

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.595
but appears to be a fully vegetarian menu.

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:19.698
For starters, we have a
vegetarian all-day breakfast.

00:13:19.698 --> 00:13:22.034
I think the main difference
is that they've subbed out

00:13:22.034 --> 00:13:25.037
the meat sausages for vegetarian sausages.

00:13:25.037 --> 00:13:27.940
It's another one that
seems to be mostly beans.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:29.842
It seems very fitting
that the British army

00:13:29.842 --> 00:13:31.243
is powered by baked beans.

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:33.646
Makes you proud to be British.

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:34.847
It's got the same issue as before,

00:13:34.847 --> 00:13:37.116
that the beans are just I think too sweet.

00:13:37.116 --> 00:13:39.451
One of the main-course
options in menu seven is

00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:42.721
the rajma masala with rice,
which I've again also had,

00:13:42.721 --> 00:13:44.223
but one that I have not had is

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:46.325
a vegetable and chickpea biryani.

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:47.526
I like a biryani.

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:51.430
For those who don't know,
it's just various things,

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.566
sometimes meat, in this case vegetables,

00:13:53.566 --> 00:13:56.669
cooked down with rice and
a bunch of Indian spices.

00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:58.871
I've had much better biryani in the past.

00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:00.873
I'm sure there are lots
of people watching at home

00:14:00.873 --> 00:14:02.408
and recoiling in horror
at the thought of this

00:14:02.408 --> 00:14:04.043
being a biryani, but it's OK,

00:14:04.043 --> 00:14:06.679
and I think on the whole,
vegetarian menu, pretty good.

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:09.481
Moving on, we have the
chicken burrito bowl,

00:14:09.481 --> 00:14:11.317
which comes in a bag and not a bowl.

00:14:11.317 --> 00:14:13.252
Sure, a lot of it's just, like ... eh, no.

00:14:13.252 --> 00:14:14.653
We got some heated up, so
you can see the difference

00:14:14.653 --> 00:14:18.057
when it's not heated up. It's
just this weird gel cube.

00:14:18.057 --> 00:14:21.327
And that comes with what
essentially would be considered

00:14:21.327 --> 00:14:25.231
a breakfast, I guess, apple
pieces in a spiced sauce.

00:14:25.231 --> 00:14:27.399
So, the entrée appears to be

00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:30.202
a maple-flavored pork sausage patty.

00:14:30.202 --> 00:14:33.339
OK, so just one block of — yep.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:38.744
Ah, it is of course just this.

00:14:38.744 --> 00:14:41.480
It's like a Clif Bar, but pork.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.382
Not good. Really weird.

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:45.417
It tastes surprisingly bland.

00:14:45.417 --> 00:14:49.321
A hash brown potato with
bacon, pepper, and onions.

00:14:49.321 --> 00:14:54.226
Ooh, no! This is the most
cat-food-y-looking one.

00:14:54.226 --> 00:14:55.628
Menu eight is another duplicate one.

00:14:55.628 --> 00:14:57.329
We start with another all-day breakfast.

00:14:57.329 --> 00:14:58.697
Then there's another chili con carne,

00:14:58.697 --> 00:15:00.866
which I've actually already
heated up and eaten.

00:15:00.866 --> 00:15:04.003
And we have another beef
burrito-style filling with rice.

00:15:04.003 --> 00:15:08.040
A cooked beef ravioli, once again.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.075
It, like, heated the bottom of it,

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:13.245
so you still gotta
massage it a little bit.

00:15:13.245 --> 00:15:14.847
Like, this side is heated,

00:15:14.847 --> 00:15:16.682
and then this middle
part didn't get heated.

00:15:16.682 --> 00:15:18.717
It also came with
tortillas, which is funny.

00:15:18.717 --> 00:15:20.419
This is what this looks
like, and it looks gross.

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:22.388
Menu nine starts with more muesli,

00:15:22.388 --> 00:15:25.157
then moves to a new dish,
which is sausage casserole.

00:15:25.157 --> 00:15:26.992
This is another classic British dish,

00:15:26.992 --> 00:15:28.227
a sausage casserole.

00:15:28.227 --> 00:15:30.462
Slow-cooked stewed sausages

00:15:30.462 --> 00:15:33.832
with tomato, potatoes, other vegetables.

00:15:33.832 --> 00:15:35.234
On the whole, the sausages
have actually been,

00:15:35.234 --> 00:15:36.602
like, surprisingly good.

00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:38.203
It might just be because I quite like

00:15:38.203 --> 00:15:41.707
those slightly cheap,
like, prepackaged sausages.

00:15:41.707 --> 00:15:42.775
And then for your other main course,

00:15:42.775 --> 00:15:44.910
we have another pindi chana aloo.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.545
This one, another hot one.

00:15:46.545 --> 00:15:49.281
Oh, so it's just going to be a patty?

00:15:49.281 --> 00:15:50.616
Ugh!

00:15:50.616 --> 00:15:51.450
Yuelei: Oh!

00:15:52.618 --> 00:15:54.453
Joe: It has a sauce, apparently.

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:57.489
It's grilled jalapeño
pepper jack flavored.

00:15:57.489 --> 00:15:59.425
Comes with au gratin potatoes.

00:16:00.793 --> 00:16:03.629
Au gratin potatoes? What
do you think of that?

00:16:03.629 --> 00:16:04.997
This looks really rough.

00:16:04.997 --> 00:16:08.467
Italian sausage with peppers,
onions in a marinara sauce.

00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:09.301
Yeah, OK.

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:12.771
Menu No. 21 should be lemon pepper tuna

00:16:12.771 --> 00:16:14.373
or tuna chunks in a bag.

00:16:14.373 --> 00:16:16.041
We've just been informed that this bag

00:16:16.041 --> 00:16:18.477
actually says white chicken
chunks, which we saw before.

00:16:18.477 --> 00:16:20.646
There is a lemon pepper
tuna that we don't have.

00:16:20.646 --> 00:16:22.715
And finally, last but not
least, we have menu 10,

00:16:22.715 --> 00:16:24.950
which starts with an instant porridge.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:26.552
The cooking instructions actually specify

00:16:26.552 --> 00:16:28.053
that you need to put boiling water in it,

00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:30.322
leave it for three minutes
to soak, and then eat it,

00:16:30.322 --> 00:16:31.490
whereas all the other ones

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.258
are technically able to be eaten cold.

00:16:33.258 --> 00:16:35.027
Menu 10 has a couple of mains,

00:16:35.027 --> 00:16:36.261
one of which is another

00:16:36.261 --> 00:16:38.530
beef burrito-style filling with rice.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:40.799
And our final main course
is hunters chicken.

00:16:40.799 --> 00:16:43.535
It's another plate one,

00:16:43.535 --> 00:16:46.171
which I don't think is a compliment.

00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:49.074
Doesn't look great, does
it? This is hunters chicken.

00:16:49.074 --> 00:16:51.543
Traditionally, this is chicken
breast with some bacon,

00:16:51.543 --> 00:16:53.479
some cheese, some barbecue sauce.

00:16:53.479 --> 00:16:55.080
I think bits of chicken in here,

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:58.484
although I'm kind of
struggling to see where.

00:16:59.651 --> 00:17:01.353
I think it's these small bits

00:17:01.353 --> 00:17:03.455
rather than, like, a chicken breast.

00:17:03.455 --> 00:17:05.524
Nah, that's really bad.

00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:07.726
Beef goulash. Beef with brown rice,

00:17:07.726 --> 00:17:10.596
spinach, carrots, tomatoes,
and smoked paprika.

00:17:10.596 --> 00:17:12.498
A pepperoni pizza and cheese slice.

00:17:14.266 --> 00:17:16.301
[groans]

00:17:16.301 --> 00:17:17.503
Army pizza.

00:17:19.872 --> 00:17:21.673
Oh, God!

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:24.043
That's so bad.

00:17:24.043 --> 00:17:25.344
This has been brutal.

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:26.612
I don't know what it is about this food.

00:17:26.612 --> 00:17:28.380
Like, yeah, some things tasted bad,

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.516
but most things just tasted OK,

00:17:30.516 --> 00:17:33.685
but I have a headache and my
stomach doesn't feel good.

00:17:33.685 --> 00:17:36.021
I noticed there's a
lot of sodium in these.

00:17:36.021 --> 00:17:37.556
So that might have
something to do with it.

00:17:37.556 --> 00:17:38.657
Tortillas came with this one,

00:17:38.657 --> 00:17:42.227
the Southwest-style beef
and black beans with sauce.

00:17:42.227 --> 00:17:44.363
Again, we have very few "breakfasts,"

00:17:44.363 --> 00:17:48.333
but this one is mixed
fruit, which appears to be,

00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:49.468
there's some chunks in there.

00:17:49.468 --> 00:17:51.737
So you got a bag of mixed fruit.

00:17:51.737 --> 00:17:53.338
On top of the mains and breakfast options,

00:17:53.338 --> 00:17:55.374
you also get a dessert
in a British ration pack.

00:17:55.374 --> 00:17:57.976
The options we got today
included a chocolate brownie,

00:17:57.976 --> 00:18:00.579
a cinnamon cake, a vanilla cake,

00:18:00.579 --> 00:18:02.281
a chocolate cake, or an orange cake.

00:18:02.281 --> 00:18:05.551
The US MREs have an
assortment of desserts,

00:18:05.551 --> 00:18:08.754
which looks all right: muffin
tops, cookies, puddings,

00:18:08.754 --> 00:18:13.725
cakes, a bun, a toaster
pastry, cookies, and cobblers.

00:18:13.725 --> 00:18:15.260
I'll try a couple of these.
I want to try the brownie

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.830
because it's packaged
differently to the others

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:19.131
and because I like brownie.

00:18:19.131 --> 00:18:21.600
It looks a little bit more
cakey than brownie-ish,

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.403
but, uh, we'll see.

00:18:24.403 --> 00:18:26.138
No. That's so dry.

00:18:26.138 --> 00:18:27.706
Starting down here,

00:18:27.706 --> 00:18:29.675
get a maple muffin top

00:18:29.675 --> 00:18:32.911
or a chocolate banana nut muffin top.

00:18:33.812 --> 00:18:35.047
Three different types of cookies.

00:18:35.047 --> 00:18:37.683
You get a oatmeal chocolate chip cookie,

00:18:37.683 --> 00:18:40.352
chocolate chip cookie, and
oatmeal cookie. That's funny.

00:18:40.352 --> 00:18:41.253
And actually, now that I think about it,

00:18:41.253 --> 00:18:42.821
we've got patriotic sugar cookies.

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:44.223
Could be in the cookie category.

00:18:44.223 --> 00:18:46.024
The packaging was different,
so I separated them,

00:18:46.024 --> 00:18:50.762
but I'm curious what a patriotic
sugar cookie looks like.

00:18:50.762 --> 00:18:52.498
Oh, no, nothing.

00:18:52.498 --> 00:18:55.300
These look like broken-up
Girl Scout cookies.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:56.869
Is that a rocket? What is that?

00:18:58.003 --> 00:18:59.738
I don't know what that is.
Do you know what that is?

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:04.309
Joe: Ah!

00:19:04.309 --> 00:19:05.444
It's the Liberty Torch.
[eagle calling]

00:19:05.444 --> 00:19:06.512
Oh, it's a bunch of different ones,

00:19:06.512 --> 00:19:08.147
but they're all broken up.

00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:10.349
Oh, well. These are pretty good.

00:19:10.349 --> 00:19:12.351
Then I wanted to try
one of the cake options.

00:19:12.351 --> 00:19:13.185
It's actually probably the cinnamon

00:19:13.185 --> 00:19:14.219
that appeals to me the most, so.

00:19:14.219 --> 00:19:15.687
I mean, this looks better.

00:19:17.489 --> 00:19:19.791
It could be, again, slightly more moist,

00:19:19.791 --> 00:19:21.460
but it's got a pretty nice texture to it.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.095
There's definitely a
cinnamon flavor there.

00:19:23.095 --> 00:19:26.598
In terms of, like,
shelf-stable baked goods,

00:19:26.598 --> 00:19:28.233
this is a much better
effort than the brownie was.

00:19:28.233 --> 00:19:30.169
This is actually perfectly edible.

00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:32.037
I have an assortment of pound cakes.

00:19:32.037 --> 00:19:35.307
Applesauce poundcake, lemon
poppy seed pound cake,

00:19:35.307 --> 00:19:38.043
vanilla pound cake, marble pound cake.

00:19:38.911 --> 00:19:41.213
Cinnamon bun

00:19:41.213 --> 00:19:43.982
and a toaster pastry

00:19:43.982 --> 00:19:45.851
that just feels completely
destroyed in here.

00:19:45.851 --> 00:19:48.253
So, I don't know what toaster

00:19:48.253 --> 00:19:49.922
you're using out in the
field, but all right.

00:19:49.922 --> 00:19:52.624
And last, this package that
looks like all the other ones

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:54.226
is a cherry blueberry cobbler.

00:19:54.226 --> 00:19:55.460
Eh, I think this'll just be fine.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.995
Oh, that's colorful.

00:19:56.995 --> 00:19:59.831
But it just looks like a
whole thing of, like, jelly.

00:19:59.831 --> 00:20:00.933
Every ration pack in the UK

00:20:00.933 --> 00:20:03.168
also comes with four
to five snack options.

00:20:03.168 --> 00:20:04.303
We've taken all of the ones we got

00:20:04.303 --> 00:20:06.238
from menus one to 10
and laid them out here.

00:20:06.238 --> 00:20:10.075
Snacks. Our US MREs come
with a lot of snacks.

00:20:10.075 --> 00:20:12.678
You usually find three or four of these

00:20:12.678 --> 00:20:16.481
in each MRE in various combinations.

00:20:16.481 --> 00:20:19.384
So, here we have a mixed-fruit snack,

00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:21.320
which is, like, a fruit puree

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.088
in one of these handy little pouches.

00:20:23.088 --> 00:20:26.792
First of all, I mean,
how bright do these look,

00:20:26.792 --> 00:20:27.993
just compared to all the packs

00:20:27.993 --> 00:20:29.361
you've been dealing with this whole video?

00:20:29.361 --> 00:20:30.262
Like, I'm looking at these,

00:20:30.262 --> 00:20:32.965
I almost want to, like,
turn the saturation down.

00:20:32.965 --> 00:20:36.101
Peppermint candy rings,
and then you got M&amp;M's,

00:20:36.101 --> 00:20:37.936
Twizzler nibs, more M&amp;M's,

00:20:37.936 --> 00:20:40.639
Skittles, Skittles, Reese's Pieces.

00:20:40.639 --> 00:20:42.241
Very nice. Thank you.

00:20:42.241 --> 00:20:43.709
There are a few different peanut options

00:20:43.709 --> 00:20:45.043
on the menus in the UK,

00:20:45.043 --> 00:20:48.447
starting with barbecue
peanuts, some chili peanuts,

00:20:48.447 --> 00:20:50.282
and the classic salted peanuts.

00:20:50.282 --> 00:20:54.753
Dried fruit, dried cranberries, raisins,

00:20:54.753 --> 00:20:57.823
and a trail mix that has ...

00:20:57.823 --> 00:20:59.858
a nut raisin mix. For the trail.

00:20:59.858 --> 00:21:02.261
Here we have cheddar cheese flavor spread.

00:21:02.261 --> 00:21:03.428
In the UK, if you're having cheese,

00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:04.997
you have cheese and crackers.

00:21:04.997 --> 00:21:07.532
So I feel like maybe this
is supposed to be enjoyed

00:21:07.532 --> 00:21:09.368
with some of these crackers down this end.

00:21:09.368 --> 00:21:12.104
Down here, three different types
of energy bars you can get.

00:21:12.104 --> 00:21:14.673
I've never heard of
the brand First Strike.

00:21:14.673 --> 00:21:15.874
Not sure if that is a brand

00:21:15.874 --> 00:21:17.909
that exists outside the military,

00:21:17.909 --> 00:21:20.245
but you can get an apple cinnamon,

00:21:20.245 --> 00:21:25.183
chocolate, or cran-raspberry energy bar.

00:21:25.183 --> 00:21:26.785
Oh, geez, look at this thing.

00:21:28.887 --> 00:21:30.422
A bunch of junk.

00:21:31.823 --> 00:21:32.691
It tastes OK.

00:21:32.691 --> 00:21:34.760
Next, we have a fruit flapjack.

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:36.662
Flapjack in the UK is a mixture

00:21:36.662 --> 00:21:39.731
of oats, syrup, butter, and often raisins,

00:21:39.731 --> 00:21:41.433
which are kind of packed together

00:21:41.433 --> 00:21:43.502
to make a nice nutritious sweet treat.

00:21:43.502 --> 00:21:46.838
This is an oatmeal block. I'm
not really sure what this is.

00:21:46.838 --> 00:21:48.006
I'm actually going to open this one

00:21:48.006 --> 00:21:49.941
just out of curiosity more than anything.

00:21:49.941 --> 00:21:53.512
Looks like a sort of shortbread
biscuit on the outside.

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:57.816
Yeah, somewhere between
a digestive biscuit

00:21:57.816 --> 00:22:01.520
and a rusk, which, for the uninitiated,

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:03.355
is I think an oaty biscuit

00:22:03.355 --> 00:22:05.023
that's basically made for babies.

00:22:05.023 --> 00:22:06.325
I feel like I used to steal rusks

00:22:06.325 --> 00:22:08.593
from my baby sister when she was little.

00:22:08.593 --> 00:22:09.428
Sorry, Annie.

00:22:09.428 --> 00:22:12.631
Trail mix, granola, nuts. You get it.

00:22:12.631 --> 00:22:14.900
Packages of either dry-roasted nuts.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:17.602
Man, they really sucked this
thing dry. Look at that.

00:22:17.602 --> 00:22:20.238
Same with this one, the smoked almonds

00:22:20.238 --> 00:22:23.041
and jalapeño cashews.

00:22:23.041 --> 00:22:26.478
Recovery trail mix with pretzels,

00:22:26.478 --> 00:22:28.580
granola,

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:30.849
and this trail mix that
has beef jerky in it.

00:22:30.849 --> 00:22:32.317
Wanna mainline your jerky?

00:22:32.317 --> 00:22:34.653
US government has you covered.

00:22:34.653 --> 00:22:36.922
Beef sticks.

00:22:36.922 --> 00:22:38.623
Here we have a sachet of peanut butter.

00:22:38.623 --> 00:22:41.026
We have three different
types of jam that we found.

00:22:41.026 --> 00:22:44.029
We have apricot, we have plum,
and we have strawberry jam.

00:22:44.029 --> 00:22:46.865
This is an exotic-fruits nougat bar.

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:48.100
Here we have a sesame bar,

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:49.401
which is basically just sesame seeds

00:22:49.401 --> 00:22:51.103
held together with melted sugar.

00:22:51.103 --> 00:22:52.771
Apricot oat biscuits.

00:22:52.771 --> 00:22:54.973
A tropical fruit and nut mix,

00:22:54.973 --> 00:22:59.444
as well as just nuts and just fruit.

00:22:59.444 --> 00:23:01.646
Cheese-filled cracker, pepperoni flavor;

00:23:02.948 --> 00:23:04.916
cheese-filled pretzel, cheddar flavor;

00:23:06.184 --> 00:23:08.086
pretzel nuggets;

00:23:08.086 --> 00:23:09.254
barbecue corn nuggets;

00:23:09.254 --> 00:23:10.622
barbecue-flavored corn kernels.

00:23:10.622 --> 00:23:12.157
So like corn nuts, right?

00:23:12.157 --> 00:23:14.092
Baked snack crackers, cheddar flavor;

00:23:14.092 --> 00:23:18.063
and the protein puffs,
ring-shaped, barbecue.

00:23:18.063 --> 00:23:19.765
I feel like if you get these
ones, you've done quite well.

00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:22.968
These sound fancy. We have
chocolate orange mini cookies

00:23:22.968 --> 00:23:25.237
and coconut biscuit bites.

00:23:25.237 --> 00:23:27.038
These sound like a more gourmet approach

00:23:27.038 --> 00:23:29.207
to a ration-pack snack.

00:23:29.207 --> 00:23:32.010
On to the breads and
spreads, we'll call it.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:35.046
Multigrain bread, white wheat snack bread,

00:23:35.046 --> 00:23:35.881
wheat snack bread.

00:23:35.881 --> 00:23:37.282
I mean, how good are the
shots we have to get of these?

00:23:37.282 --> 00:23:38.116
Everything looks the same.

00:23:38.116 --> 00:23:40.152
And then this one, Italian
bread blobbity blob.

00:23:40.152 --> 00:23:41.453
Got it. OK, great.

00:23:41.453 --> 00:23:44.489
You have a vegetable cracker
or a regular cracker.

00:23:44.489 --> 00:23:46.124
What do you want to put on
those breads or crackers?

00:23:46.124 --> 00:23:49.027
You got chunky peanut
butter, peanut butter,

00:23:49.027 --> 00:23:50.929
chocolate peanut spread,

00:23:50.929 --> 00:23:53.198
cheese bread, cheese
spread with jalapeños,

00:23:54.166 --> 00:23:55.500
cheese spread with bacon.

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:57.302
Here we have cheese and oat biscuits,

00:23:57.302 --> 00:23:58.770
which I think are probably
designed, like I say,

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.272
to be eaten with the cheesy spread.

00:24:00.272 --> 00:24:02.073
Next up, our biscuit browns.

00:24:02.073 --> 00:24:03.842
I wasn't sure what a biscuit brown was,

00:24:03.842 --> 00:24:06.578
and after tasting it, I'm
still kind of equally unsure.

00:24:06.578 --> 00:24:08.079
It's, like, a sort of brown, like,

00:24:08.079 --> 00:24:10.348
wheaty cracker-type thing.

00:24:10.348 --> 00:24:14.386
For the fruit, you got
apple jelly, strawberry jam,

00:24:14.386 --> 00:24:15.987
and I know there was a
grape jelly from earlier.

00:24:15.987 --> 00:24:16.822
I don't know where it went.

00:24:16.822 --> 00:24:18.957
But it looks exactly like this package.

00:24:18.957 --> 00:24:21.626
And finally, we have a
cookies and cream bar.

00:24:21.626 --> 00:24:23.728
[laughs] That's not what
I was expecting at all.

00:24:23.728 --> 00:24:25.430
When you hear cookies and cream,

00:24:25.430 --> 00:24:27.432
I'm right in thinking that
you expect Oreo, right?

00:24:27.432 --> 00:24:31.470
Whereas this is more like a
rice crispy type of treat.

00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:33.271
Doesn't smell of Oreo at all.

00:24:33.271 --> 00:24:35.640
It literally smells of
a rice crispy treat,

00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:37.309
maybe dark chocolate.

00:24:37.309 --> 00:24:38.510
Doesn't taste great either.

00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:41.413
The US MREs have an assortment
of different drinks,

00:24:41.413 --> 00:24:44.583
both I guess regular temperature and warm.

00:24:44.583 --> 00:24:46.318
So, the first thing I want
to do before we get into that

00:24:46.318 --> 00:24:48.386
is point out that we have four different,

00:24:48.386 --> 00:24:50.388
in the middle here, coffee drinks,

00:24:50.388 --> 00:24:52.624
hot drinks, as you will have it.

00:24:52.624 --> 00:24:55.060
This is a French vanilla cappuccino. Mm.

00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:57.062
And I want to make it real quick.

00:24:57.062 --> 00:24:59.097
And we saw how we heated
up the drinks before, so.

00:24:59.097 --> 00:25:01.032
Here it also comes with
a hot beverage bag.

00:25:01.032 --> 00:25:02.400
Pre-added the water.

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:05.270
So now I'm going to go ahead and put

00:25:06.872 --> 00:25:08.373
powder in here.

00:25:09.441 --> 00:25:11.676
This looks all right.
Mix it up a little bit.

00:25:12.677 --> 00:25:16.314
♪ I have me cappuccino ♪

00:25:20.151 --> 00:25:22.020
It smells like when the
VCR gets really hot,

00:25:22.020 --> 00:25:23.755
when you watch, like,
three movies in a row.

00:25:23.755 --> 00:25:25.290
Now we're on to the drink
options, which, again,

00:25:25.290 --> 00:25:28.260
I think you get four of in a
24-hour British ration pack.

00:25:28.260 --> 00:25:29.761
These all come in the form of powders,

00:25:29.761 --> 00:25:31.563
which you mix with water and then consume.

00:25:31.563 --> 00:25:33.398
They're also split into
four different categories.

00:25:33.398 --> 00:25:35.700
We have just a standard drink powder,

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:37.469
we have an energy drink powder,

00:25:37.469 --> 00:25:39.371
a fortified energy drink powder,

00:25:39.371 --> 00:25:41.840
and we have an isotonic drink powder.

00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:43.975
Having quickly scanned the
ingredients of both of these,

00:25:43.975 --> 00:25:45.544
I'm actually not sure what
the difference is between,

00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:47.212
say, an energy drink powder

00:25:47.212 --> 00:25:49.447
and a standard fruit-flavor powder.

00:25:49.447 --> 00:25:52.050
There's no caffeine in the
energy powders, for example.

00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:53.318
I think most of the energy is coming from

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:54.819
the sugar content in these.

00:25:54.819 --> 00:25:59.324
While that's cooking, let's
see what other drinks we have.

00:25:59.324 --> 00:26:01.593
We got orange, lemon-lime, and grape.

00:26:01.593 --> 00:26:05.263
That's definitely not grape
colored. It says grape on here.

00:26:06.965 --> 00:26:09.034
I think it tastes like grape,
but also because it's blue,

00:26:09.034 --> 00:26:10.502
I'm thinking blue raspberry.

00:26:10.502 --> 00:26:12.203
While my coffee is cooking,

00:26:12.203 --> 00:26:14.372
I also have different coffee flavors.

00:26:14.372 --> 00:26:18.643
I get a chocolate hazelnut protein drink,

00:26:18.643 --> 00:26:21.947
Irish cream cappuccino,
chocolate protein drink.

00:26:21.947 --> 00:26:23.748
Regardless of the type of drink
powder that you're getting,

00:26:23.748 --> 00:26:25.984
they do come in a bunch of
different flavor options.

00:26:25.984 --> 00:26:28.787
I'm not sure if any of these
particularly appeal to me.

00:26:28.787 --> 00:26:29.854
I'll try the tutti-frutti one.

00:26:29.854 --> 00:26:32.390
I feel like of all of
these, sounds pretty fun.

00:26:32.390 --> 00:26:34.092
Yeah, I was really hoping
that the color would be, like,

00:26:34.092 --> 00:26:37.762
a bright blue or pink or
something, but just normal.

00:26:40.131 --> 00:26:42.267
It's unlocking some kind of, like,

00:26:42.267 --> 00:26:44.803
repressed alcohol memory, I think.

00:26:44.803 --> 00:26:47.906
I'm fairly sure I've drunk a cocktail

00:26:47.906 --> 00:26:50.408
to the point of oblivion that
tasted pretty much like this.

00:26:50.408 --> 00:26:55.246
So, this is my French vanilla coffee.

00:27:00.752 --> 00:27:01.586
Oh, yeah.

00:27:01.586 --> 00:27:04.289
I'm not recognizing a lot of these words,

00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:05.490
but yeah, this is nice.

00:27:05.490 --> 00:27:09.961
And the last thing we have
here are beverage base powders.

00:27:09.961 --> 00:27:12.998
So, these had electrolytes in them.

00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:14.499
It's like energy drinks almost.

00:27:14.499 --> 00:27:16.568
And then these, I think, are just,

00:27:16.568 --> 00:27:18.203
these have lots of sugar in them.

00:27:18.203 --> 00:27:22.941
So, we have lemon-lime,
orange, and tropical punch,

00:27:22.941 --> 00:27:24.709
and then this little stick,

00:27:24.709 --> 00:27:26.978
beverage base, orange type three.

00:27:26.978 --> 00:27:28.680
Finally, every ration pack in the UK

00:27:28.680 --> 00:27:30.715
also contains a bag of common items.

00:27:33.451 --> 00:27:36.087
We'll start down this end,
where we have some matches.

00:27:36.087 --> 00:27:38.857
Then we have some
water-purification tablets.

00:27:38.857 --> 00:27:40.925
I think there are six of
these in here, actually.

00:27:40.925 --> 00:27:41.860
And according to this,

00:27:41.860 --> 00:27:44.229
you can purify a liter
of water per tablet.

00:27:44.229 --> 00:27:45.063
That's pretty good.

00:27:45.063 --> 00:27:46.998
I like that this is in
the essential-items thing.

00:27:46.998 --> 00:27:48.133
We have some hot sauce.

00:27:48.133 --> 00:27:50.068
We have some tissues,

00:27:50.068 --> 00:27:53.004
as well as two alcohol-free hand wipes.

00:27:53.004 --> 00:27:56.441
Then you have two tea bags,
two sachets of instant coffee,

00:27:56.441 --> 00:27:59.077
four sachets of beverage whitener.

00:27:59.077 --> 00:28:01.312
I think, again, this might be
something along the lines of

00:28:01.312 --> 00:28:03.415
they can't legally call
this powdered milk,

00:28:03.415 --> 00:28:05.717
but it is effectively a
powdered-milk substitute.

00:28:05.717 --> 00:28:08.119
And four sachets of sugar.

00:28:08.119 --> 00:28:11.089
Our US MREs have these
following accessories.

00:28:11.089 --> 00:28:12.123
First of all, over here,

00:28:12.123 --> 00:28:16.695
you've seen it a few times this
episode, the heating thing,

00:28:16.695 --> 00:28:19.297
the heating bags to heat up
your food and your drinks.

00:28:19.297 --> 00:28:21.166
Saw this the whole time, the spoon.

00:28:21.166 --> 00:28:23.568
Every MRE comes with a spoon.

00:28:23.568 --> 00:28:26.371
Now, did you notice I had a difficult time

00:28:26.371 --> 00:28:28.173
kind of cutting into some
stuff? And I thought,

00:28:28.173 --> 00:28:30.008
why don't they have anything
like a knife in here?

00:28:30.008 --> 00:28:30.909
Of course they have a knife.

00:28:30.909 --> 00:28:33.344
They're soldiers. They have pocket knives.

00:28:33.344 --> 00:28:36.481
They come with a
concentrated beverage base.

00:28:36.481 --> 00:28:38.783
This one is cranberry grape.

00:28:38.783 --> 00:28:41.219
Over here is the coffee
zone, for the most part.

00:28:41.219 --> 00:28:43.755
Bill's Brew freeze-dried coffee.

00:28:43.755 --> 00:28:45.990
You can add it to hot or cold water.

00:28:45.990 --> 00:28:47.292
6 ounces right here.

00:28:47.292 --> 00:28:49.794
And you have your choice
of either Splenda or sugar.

00:28:49.794 --> 00:28:52.831
Salt, if you need more
sodium on your food.

00:28:52.831 --> 00:28:54.466
This is a coffee creamer.

00:28:54.466 --> 00:28:56.701
Each pack of accessories
comes with two pieces of gum.

00:28:56.701 --> 00:28:58.837
These are waterproof matches.

00:28:58.837 --> 00:29:01.306
Spice up that food a little
bit, a little bit of Tabasco.

00:29:01.306 --> 00:29:05.343
A little Tabasco guy. Look
at this little guy. Right?

00:29:05.343 --> 00:29:08.913
A moist towelette and regular napkins.

00:29:12.250 --> 00:29:15.253
In the US, MREs were first
introduced in the 1980s

00:29:15.253 --> 00:29:17.489
and were designed to be
lightweight, portable,

00:29:17.489 --> 00:29:18.723
and self-contained meals

00:29:18.723 --> 00:29:20.959
that didn't require
cooking or refrigeration.

00:29:20.959 --> 00:29:23.995
They were also intended to
provide the necessary nutrition

00:29:23.995 --> 00:29:25.330
for soldiers in the field.

00:29:25.330 --> 00:29:26.931
Early iterations of British ration packs

00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:28.233
actually used cans.

00:29:28.233 --> 00:29:29.667
It wasn't until the 1990s

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.202
that these were replaced with pouches.

00:29:31.202 --> 00:29:35.106
Each MRE typically contains
around 1,200 to 1,300 calories

00:29:35.106 --> 00:29:38.610
with balanced nutrition essential
to supporting the demands

00:29:38.610 --> 00:29:41.212
placed on soldiers during
military operations.

00:29:41.212 --> 00:29:43.047
Each MRE is said to have approximately

00:29:43.047 --> 00:29:44.983
170 grams of carbohydrates,

00:29:44.983 --> 00:29:48.052
45 grams of protein, and 50 grams of fat.

00:29:48.052 --> 00:29:50.388
As we've said, a British
ration pack is usually designed

00:29:50.388 --> 00:29:52.557
for 24 hours' worth of nutrition,

00:29:52.557 --> 00:29:54.626
whereas it seems as if
the American ones are not.

00:29:54.626 --> 00:29:57.061
We can assume this because
the average nutritional value

00:29:57.061 --> 00:29:58.563
of an entire British ration pack

00:29:58.563 --> 00:30:02.066
is somewhere between
3,800 and 4,200 calories.

00:30:02.066 --> 00:30:03.868
Now, here's a chili meal from before.

00:30:03.868 --> 00:30:05.870
We're going to go through
its specific nutrition.

00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:06.704
Now, I want to point out

00:30:06.704 --> 00:30:09.040
that the bag didn't have anything on it,

00:30:09.040 --> 00:30:13.678
so I am learning about the
nutrition of these in real time.

00:30:13.678 --> 00:30:16.347
The chili with the
beans, one serving size.

00:30:16.347 --> 00:30:18.950
All this is 260 calories.

00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:20.919
And this single serving of cornbread

00:30:20.919 --> 00:30:24.355
with your chili, also 260 calories.

00:30:24.355 --> 00:30:27.292
Your vegetable cracker is
going to be 170 calories,

00:30:27.292 --> 00:30:31.529
and your cheesy spread is 120 calories.

00:30:31.529 --> 00:30:34.299
Then the cheese-filled crackers,
the pepperoni pizza flavor,

00:30:34.299 --> 00:30:36.901
240 calories for this one.

00:30:36.901 --> 00:30:38.603
And if you're going to be sipping on your

00:30:38.603 --> 00:30:41.940
lemon-lime-flavored non-fruit-juice juice,

00:30:41.940 --> 00:30:44.976
that's going to be 130 calories
for the whole beverage.

00:30:44.976 --> 00:30:47.545
A grand total of this many calories.

00:30:47.545 --> 00:30:49.681
We've selected some items
which seem to match up roughly

00:30:49.681 --> 00:30:51.950
with what you'd expect
to find in a US MRE.

00:30:51.950 --> 00:30:54.085
Here we have the chili con carne main.

00:30:54.085 --> 00:30:56.221
We've got some crackers
with the cheese spread,

00:30:56.221 --> 00:30:59.390
some peanut butter, and
a fruit-flavored drink.

00:30:59.390 --> 00:31:02.961
The total calories for
these items comes to 1,379.

00:31:02.961 --> 00:31:04.596
The FDA recommends that adults consume

00:31:04.596 --> 00:31:07.966
around 75 to 90 milligrams
of vitamin C per day.

00:31:07.966 --> 00:31:09.234
Just two of these drink sachets

00:31:09.234 --> 00:31:11.302
is more than enough
vitamin C for that intake.

00:31:11.302 --> 00:31:12.637
We are not getting scurvy anymore.

00:31:12.637 --> 00:31:14.405
We learned our lessons
back in the navy days.

00:31:14.405 --> 00:31:15.406
Although it's also worth noting

00:31:15.406 --> 00:31:16.975
the amount of sugar
that is in one of these.

00:31:16.975 --> 00:31:20.478
In a 45-gram sachet of mango
and passion fruit drink,

00:31:20.478 --> 00:31:23.414
you will find 40.5 grams of sugar.

00:31:23.414 --> 00:31:25.850
That's 81% of your daily
recommended intake,

00:31:25.850 --> 00:31:26.951
just in one of these.

00:31:29.187 --> 00:31:30.188
Let's take a look at the ingredients

00:31:30.188 --> 00:31:32.056
of the chili con carne in the UK.

00:31:32.056 --> 00:31:36.661
Beef, red kidney beans,
tomato puree, water, onion,

00:31:36.661 --> 00:31:39.898
red and green peppers, wheat
flour, calcium carbonate,

00:31:39.898 --> 00:31:43.635
iron, thiamine, and nicotinamide,
modified maize starch,

00:31:43.635 --> 00:31:46.237
salt, spices, spice extracts,

00:31:46.237 --> 00:31:48.273
calcium carbonate, and smoke flavor.

00:31:48.273 --> 00:31:50.441
The ingredients in here are
actually all pretty natural,

00:31:50.441 --> 00:31:52.543
without any real artificial preservatives.

00:31:52.543 --> 00:31:53.611
Our eyebrows were raised

00:31:53.611 --> 00:31:55.847
when we saw nicotinamide
in the wheat flour.

00:31:55.847 --> 00:31:57.482
Thankfully, it's not
some kind of nicotine,

00:31:57.482 --> 00:32:00.652
it's just another type of
vitamin B3, aka niacin.

00:32:00.652 --> 00:32:04.188
This chili with beans contains all this.

00:32:04.188 --> 00:32:06.024
Looks like mostly normal stuff

00:32:06.024 --> 00:32:07.592
until you get the bottom
of the list there.

00:32:07.592 --> 00:32:11.462
Ethoxylated mono- diglycerides,
I have no idea what that is.

00:32:11.462 --> 00:32:13.031
I don't think we've ever had
that in "Food Wars" before.

00:32:13.031 --> 00:32:15.667
So if someone in editing can go ahead

00:32:15.667 --> 00:32:17.802
and say what it's used for ...

00:32:17.802 --> 00:32:20.271
These have a minimum
shelf life of three years,

00:32:20.271 --> 00:32:22.173
depending on storage conditions.

00:32:22.173 --> 00:32:23.875
The storage conditions for these MREs

00:32:23.875 --> 00:32:26.611
I'm assuming were room
temperature the whole time,

00:32:26.611 --> 00:32:31.149
so I'm feeling pretty confident
these are all not expired.

00:32:31.149 --> 00:32:33.685
Similarly, ours have a shelf
life of around three years,

00:32:33.685 --> 00:32:35.253
and after that, it's
down to the temperature

00:32:35.253 --> 00:32:36.154
at which they're stored.

00:32:36.154 --> 00:32:39.090
For example, this chili
was made in December 2021

00:32:39.090 --> 00:32:42.093
and apparently is shelf
stable until around 2025.

00:32:42.093 --> 00:32:43.428
"But how can these meals have

00:32:43.428 --> 00:32:45.964
such a long shelf life?" you ask.

00:32:45.964 --> 00:32:47.198
According to the USDA,

00:32:47.198 --> 00:32:50.168
MREs are shelf stable
because they have been

00:32:50.168 --> 00:32:52.904
commercially sterilized by heat

00:32:52.904 --> 00:32:55.106
in a sealed container to destroy bacteria

00:32:55.106 --> 00:32:57.809
that can make it unsafe or spoil the food.

00:32:57.809 --> 00:32:59.911
Like food in metal cans,

00:32:59.911 --> 00:33:03.781
MREs can be kept for a long
time, but not indefinitely.

00:33:03.781 --> 00:33:05.583
The shelf life of MREs and ration packs

00:33:05.583 --> 00:33:06.651
is pretty directly related

00:33:06.651 --> 00:33:08.519
to the temperature at
which they're stored.

00:33:08.519 --> 00:33:09.821
The cooler the storage temperature,

00:33:09.821 --> 00:33:10.922
the longer they'll last.

00:33:10.922 --> 00:33:12.290
Rations in a desert temperature

00:33:12.290 --> 00:33:13.725
might only last a few months,

00:33:13.725 --> 00:33:16.194
whereas rations at room
temperature or colder climates

00:33:16.194 --> 00:33:18.096
can be good up to five years.

00:33:18.096 --> 00:33:20.098
We're filming this
towards the end of 2023,

00:33:20.098 --> 00:33:22.000
which means that our chili
con carne, for example,

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:23.935
is already around two years old.

00:33:23.935 --> 00:33:26.004
I've gotta say, I don't feel
great after eating them.

00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:27.739
However, I do think
that's probably more due

00:33:27.739 --> 00:33:29.140
to the quantity that I've eaten

00:33:29.140 --> 00:33:32.010
rather than due to the
storage quality of these.

00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:34.912
Since 1981, the US menu has
changed about five times,

00:33:34.912 --> 00:33:36.414
improving the quality and the taste.

00:33:36.414 --> 00:33:38.783
It also has expanded the menu variety

00:33:38.783 --> 00:33:42.420
and now includes vegetarian,
kosher, and halal options.

00:33:42.420 --> 00:33:44.222
There also aren't many changes in the UK.

00:33:44.222 --> 00:33:46.491
However, there was a recent
controversial change.

00:33:46.491 --> 00:33:48.159
Chocolate bars were taken
away from British troops

00:33:48.159 --> 00:33:49.727
serving in Iraq and Afghanistan

00:33:49.727 --> 00:33:51.462
because they kept melting
in the desert heat.

00:33:51.462 --> 00:33:54.332
They were replaced with the
much less popular peanut butter.

00:33:54.332 --> 00:33:55.867
I can see how people would
be annoyed about that.

00:33:55.867 --> 00:33:58.703
So, you get five matches

00:33:59.937 --> 00:34:02.740
as well as one of these
little striking strips.

00:34:07.612 --> 00:34:10.048
I broke it, so, whoopsy daisy.

